event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"## 1\n\nMan, I’m so sorry. If it’s reached"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" the point where you want to walk out tomorrow, it must be completely draining you. \n\nI’m 100% in"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" your corner whatever you choose, but before you pull the trigger, do you want to grab dinner or jump on a call tonight? Even"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" if you still decide to resign tomorrow, it might help to vent it all out first so you can walk away on your own terms with"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" a clear head. \n\nI’m free tonight—let me know.\n\n## 2\n\nI hear where you’re coming from"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" regarding skepticism about institutional images, but we actually don't need satellite photos or modern space agencies to know the Earth is a"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" curved sphere. People figured that out thousands of years ago using simple, repeatable observations anyone can verify.\n\nFor instance, during a lunar"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" eclipse, the Earth casts a shadow on the Moon, and that shadow is always circular—something only a sphere can produce regardless"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" of orientation. Or consider travel: if you fly south toward the equator and past it, constellations like the North Star disappear below the horizon"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":", while entirely new constellations, like the Southern Cross, rise into view. That shift wouldn’t happen on a flat plane"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":". Even the fact that ships disappear bottom-first over the horizon, or that time zones exist with the sun rising in"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" Tokyo while it’s dark in New York, relies entirely on curvature. \n\nI’m always open to questioning"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" assumptions, but the sheer weight of everyday geometry and physics points to a round Earth.\n\n## 3\n\nTo understand why the sky is blue"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":", we first have to look at sunlight. Even though sunlight looks white or yellowish to us, it’s actually a mix of every color"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" in the rainbow, all traveling together in waves.\n\nEach color travels in a different wave size. Red and orange have long, lazy"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" wavelengths, while blue and violet have short, choppy ones.\n\nWhen sunlight hits Earth’s atmosphere, it crashes into a sea"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" of invisible gas molecules (mostly nitrogen and oxygen). The long waves, like red and yellow, mostly pass straight through without bumping into much"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":". But the short, choppy blue waves smack right into those tiny gas molecules and bounce off in every possible direction. "}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\nScientists call this **Rayleigh scattering**. Because blue light gets scattered and bounced around across the entire atmosphere, whenever you"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" look up away from the sun, your eyes are catching that scattered blue light coming from every angle. \n\n(And"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" if you're wondering why the sky isn't violet—since violet light has even shorter waves—it's because the"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" sun emits much more blue light than violet, and human eyes happen to be far more sensitive to blue.)\n\n## 4\n\n窗外的"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"雨淅淅沥沥地下着，将整座城市的霓虹晕染成一片朦胧的光斑。夜深了"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"，潮湿的柏油路面上倒映着清冷而昏黄的路灯光影，偶尔有车辆"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"疾驰而过，激起一阵短暂的白雾与水花。雨滴持续敲打着窗玻璃，"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"节奏轻缓而细密，像是在低声诉说。风卷着丝丝凉意从窗缝钻"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"进来，夹杂着泥土的气息。屋内暖黄的灯光安静地亮着，茶杯里余"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"热未散，把窗外的寒凉与喧嚣悄然隔绝在另一个世界。\n\n## 5\n\n"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"Subject: Re: Friday team drinks\n\nHi [Name],\n\nThanks so much for organizing this! Unfortunately, I won"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"’t be able to make it this Friday due to a prior commitment. \n\nI hope you all have a great"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" time unwinding, and I’ll definitely catch you at the next one.\n\nBest,  \n[Your Name]\n\n## "}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"6\n\nMy writing style is clear, adaptable, and direct, focused on communicating complex ideas with precision while adopting an authentic"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":", context-appropriate tone."}}

